  "notes": [
    "弟弟: lexical colloquial changed tone on the second syllable does not affect the tone-free spelling dai dai. The per-character dictionary reading is dai6.",
    "即刻: use zik hak, not zik haak; CUHK hak1 is the main supported reading.",
    "弄髒手 is recommended over 手髒 in the five-slot pattern 人物＋一＋事情①＋就＋事情②. 我一弄髒手，就洗手 reads more naturally than 我一手髒，就洗手. The same picture can be retained. CUHK uses lung6 for 弄; nung6 is an alternative reading.",
    "穿雨傘 and 喝鞋子 are intentionally mismatched verb-object phrases; label 不合理 against ordinary real-life usage, and illustrate the specific mismatch. They are not a general basis for marking unusual but physically possible daily routines wrong.",
    "穿雨傘: putting umbrella(s) on as footwear communicates wrong object for 穿; show normal shoes as the visual repair. 喝鞋子: shoe is a solid object, not a drink; show a glass of water as repair.",
    "Natural spoken audio must preserve the words on each Chinese card. Do not silently read 喝水 as 飲水 while showing hot seoi, or 吃飯 as 食飯 while showing hek faan."
  ]
